4916	  // AST visitors.  We start by adding a visitor callback for
4917	  // most of the subclasses of Decl/Stmt/Type listed in:
4918	  //   clang/AST/DeclNodes.def
4919	  //   clang/AST/StmtNodes.td
4920	  //   clang/AST/TypeNodes.def
4921	  // We exclude only:
4922	  //   1) abstract declarations and types with no logic (e.g. NamedDecl)
4923	  //   2) ObjC declarations, statements, and types (e.g. ObjcIvarDecl)
4924	  // RecursiveASTVisitor defines specialized visitors for each specific
4925	  // math operation (MulAssign, OffsetOf, etc).  We don't override
4926	  // those callbacks, but use their default behavior, which is to call
4927	  // back to VisitUnaryOperator, VisitBinaryOperator, etc.
4928	  //
4929	  // Over time, as we understand when a callback is called and
4930	  // which can be ignored by iwyu, we will pare down the list.
4931	  //   Each of these returns a bool: false if we want to abort the
4932	  // traversal (we never do).  For Visit*(), we can abort early if
4933	  // we're not in the main compilation-unit, since we only ever give
4934	  // iwyu warnings on symbols in those files.
